{"availability":"available","full":"connectrpc/connect-go","name":"connect-go","description":"The Go implementation of Connect: Protobuf RPC that works.","category":"Other","language":"Go","stars":4123,"forks":158,"created":"2021-08-02T04:08:04Z","updated":"2026-10-19T21:23:39Z","license":"Apache-2.0","branch":"main","homepage":"https://connectrpc.com","topics":["connectrpc","go","grpc","protobuf","rpc"],"demo":"https://demo.connectrpc.com/","color":"#25392f","ink":"#d1e5c5","lastCheckedAt":"2026-10-20T01:50:41.664Z","lastAttemptAt":"2026-10-20T01:50:41.664Z","lastAvailableAt":"2026-10-20T01:50:41.664Z","metrics":[{"at":"2026-10-05T19:23:23.864Z","stars":4101,"forks":158},{"at":"2026-10-07T20:13:49.694Z","stars":4104,"forks":158},{"at":"2026-10-08T16:05:52.751Z","stars":4108,"forks":158},{"at":"2026-10-09T23:11:17.931Z","stars":4109,"forks":157},{"at":"2026-10-15T11:19:50.926Z","stars":4119,"forks":158},{"at":"2026-10-19T09:31:39.761Z","stars":4122,"forks":158},{"at":"2026-10-20T01:50:41.664Z","stars":4123,"forks":158}],"technologies":["Go"],"overview":{"kind":"readme","version":1,"paragraphs":["Connect is a slim library for building browser and gRPC-compatible HTTP APIs. You write a short Protocol Buffer schema and implement your application logic, and Connect generates code to handle marshaling, routing, compression, and content type negotiation. It also generates an idiomatic, type-safe client. Handlers and clients support three protocols: gRPC, gRPC-Web, and Connect's own protocol.","The Connect protocol is a simple protocol that works over HTTP/1.1 or HTTP/2. It takes the best portions of gRPC and gRPC-Web, including streaming, and packages them into a protocol that works equally well in browsers, monoliths, and microservices. Calling a Connect API is as easy as using curl. Try it with our live demo:","Handlers and clients also support the gRPC and gRPC-Web protocols, including streaming, headers, trailers, and error details. gRPC-compatible server reflection and health checks are available as standalone packages. Instead of cURL, we could call our API with a gRPC client:"],"features":[],"sourceUrl":"https://github.com/connectrpc/connect-go/blob/main/README.md","fingerprint":"7195a26fda589181b0e707376293dcbec4e4b10b4b96387e623c9124647ff0ef","extractedAt":"2026-10-07T21:26:19.845Z"},"overviewCheckedAt":"2026-10-20T01:50:41.727Z","projectInsights":{"version":1,"whatItDoes":{"text":"Connect is a slim library for building browser and gRPC-compatible HTTP APIs. You write a short Protocol Buffer schema and implement your application logic, and Connect generates code to handle marshaling, routing, compression, and content type negotiation. It also generates an idiomatic, type-safe client. Handlers and clients support three protocols: gRPC, gRPC-Web, and Connect's own protocol.","sourceUrl":"https://github.com/connectrpc/connect-go/blob/main/README.md"},"audience":[],"requirements":[],"fingerprint":"7195a26fda589181b0e707376293dcbec4e4b10b4b96387e623c9124647ff0ef","sourceUrl":"https://github.com/connectrpc/connect-go/blob/main/README.md","checkedAt":"2026-10-20T01:50:41.727Z"},"overviewRepoUpdated":"2026-10-19T21:23:39Z","readmeSnapshot":{"version":1,"status":"saved","sourceUrl":"https://github.com/connectrpc/connect-go/blob/main/README.md","checkedAt":"2026-10-20T01:50:41.728Z","hash":"7195a26fda589181b0e707376293dcbec4e4b10b4b96387e623c9124647ff0ef","originalBytes":7519,"storedBytes":7519,"truncated":false},"lastDemoCheckedAt":"2026-10-20T01:50:41.664Z","enrichmentAttemptAt":"2026-10-05T19:23:40.719Z","latestRelease":{"name":"v1.21.0","tag":"v1.21.0","publishedAt":"2026-09-08T13:40:12Z","url":"https://github.com/connectrpc/connect-go/releases/tag/v1.21.0"},"releaseCheckedAt":"2026-10-05T19:23:40.719Z","screenshots":[{"src":"previews/affa074345a1e73bebfbc406.jpg","kind":"demo","capturedAt":"2026-10-20T02:04:37.688Z","url":"https://demo.connectrpc.com/"}],"demoHealth":{"url":"https://demo.connectrpc.com/","attemptedAt":"2026-10-2